// E0302 with one candidate: the head of a `use` is a name that a `use` of this module took (§15.1, S-37).
// The candidate is the path of the binding in front of the rest: `util.counter` was taken as `counter`,
// so `use counter.{next}` becomes `use util.counter.{next}`. The package `std` was taken as the module
// `std.math`, so `use math.{sin}` is `use std.math.{sin}` (via_std.onsa) and the whole list stays in the
// candidate (`use math.{sin, cos}` in via_std_list.onsa). The `use` lines that took the names are not changed.

use util.counter

use util.counter.{next}                                  //~ E0302

